                <pb facs="0758" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.516/208</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 924</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegram No. 925, March 28, 6 p.m., relative to the objection raised by the
                    French Government to Article 10 of the law governing the Mexican bank of issue,
                    I have the honor to report that it is apparent that nothing may be accomplished
                    at this time by individual or joint protest, and for this reason I suggest that
                    no representations be made at present.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
